    {
      "ordinal": 2,
      "depth": 0,
      "kind": "section",
      "number": "1",
      "title": "Definition",
      "body": "If we read the current rules, if a fighter enters the list with equipment (armor, shield, or weapon) that fails the authenticity check, he/she receives a green card the fighter enters the list but only once per tournament.\n\nAuthenticity Committee think this rule is too punishing as we understand some fighters are not supported by any authenticity committee members, or have difficulties to purchase armor that match aesthetic standards of Buhurt International. Therefore, we would like to propose both clarification and softening of how authenticity rules are applied.\n\nAuthenticity rules are meant to be followed by all competitors attending Buhurt International tournaments, no matter the category. If a competitor shows up with an armor, shield or weapon that does not comply with the Authenticity rules, he/she risks a penalty.",
      "page_from": 3,
      "page_to": 3,
      "stable_key": "infractions:1",
      "parent_key": null,
      "review_status": "extracted",
      "review_note": null,
